#! ia 1.0

@system ia-authoring-catalogue
  provider "local"
  version "0.1.0"
  describes "The catalogue-authoring part of the IA authoring kit: the house rules a plugin catalogue enforces on every plugin, restated as conventions, one capability with its playbook for bringing a plugin inside them, and the check that runs the catalogue's validator. It is used with the host-authoring part, whose host-qualify activity qualifies the plugin on its hosts. This system mints no words and grants no authority."
  steward @agent catalogue-authoring-steward
  requires
    - agent-system
    - agent-composition-system
    - workspace-system
    - governance-system
    - compliance-system

@agent catalogue-authoring-steward
  meaning
    says "Owns the records of the IA authoring kit's catalogue-authoring part and reviews every change to them."
    answers "Who owns the catalogue-authoring part of the IA authoring kit?"
  governance
    applies [convention, playbook, capability, contract, check, case]
